{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If 554 is the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> representation of the square of the number whose base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> representation is 24, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, when written in base 10, equals \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/0479ae228fa437d55dc18c781def4c8d7ece2854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 12\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 14\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Write out the numbers using the definition of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base_numbers\" title=\"Base numbers\">base numbers</a>.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4cb439c4b096a30dc579d5dcdf0e2e3e134f72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[554_b = 5b^2 + 5b + 4\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/226ed8b9f9ee0f6b01979a8aa9b87ae64dfc5e65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24_b = 2b+4\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c4de18a1af3e6dedc4698092d3b3d492142f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$554_b = (24_b)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" />, we can write an equation.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a74a076030848e89544a94de652ea2d04e5fcb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5b^2 + 5b + 4 = (2b+4)^2\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/6014c8d6ddcd262b3daf255578b7de0d8618d5a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5b^2 + 5b + 4 = 4b^2 + 16b + 16\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/020d7c07e6faefc93544f0e9d9404da39a1e8fc9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2 - 11b - 12 = 0\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/345a0162726a105dffb09838f61b2df5f4098b9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(b-12)(b+1) = 0\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />\nSince base numbers must be positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in base 10 equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af8237179d4a7a4d75a63ed5f39f7fdae43636ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Se